description.narrative:
Depuis juillet 2023, le consortium MDF – VNG-International – Kadaster International et l’Agence nationale du Domaine et du Foncier (ANDF) exécute le Projet de Préparation de la Mise à l’Echelle du Cadastre national (PPMEC) au Bénin. A quelques mois du terme de ce projet, ces parties se sont concertées pour solliciter la poursuite des interventions du projet. Cette demande est motivée notamment par le désir de :
•	Pérenniser les acquis obtenus et éviter que les résultats issus des efforts conjugués des différents acteurs impliqués, ne soient perdus ;
•	Poursuivre l’accompagnement des douze (12) Communes d’intervention dans la mise à jour des données cadastrales ;
•	Assurer le renforcement des capacités de l’ANDF en vue d’une prise en mains totale de la gestion et de la maintenance de e-Foncier Bénin ;
•	Réaliser la couverture intégrale de deux (02) nouvelles Communes PMAF/PPMEC en données cadastrales, à l’instar de celle de Cotonou.

Since July 2023, the consortium MDF - VNG-International - Kadaster International and the Agence nationale du Domaine et du Foncier (ANDF) has been implementing the Project to Prepare for the Scaling-up of the National Land Registry (PPMEC) in Benin. With a few months to go before the end of this project, these parties have come together to request the continuation of the project's interventions. This request is motivated in particular by the desire to:
•    Sustain the achievements obtained and prevent the results of the combined efforts of the various actors involved from being lost;
•    Continue to support the twelve (12) municipalities involved in updating cadastral data;
•    Ensure the strengthening of the capacities of the ANDF with a view to taking full control of the management and maintenance of e-Foncier Bénin;
•    Achieve full coverage of two (02) new PMAF/PPMEC Communes in cadastral data, following the example of Cotonou.
The ambition of the Government of Benin and the ANDF is to scale up the land registry throughout the country, according to the model implemented in the 12 PPMEC communes.

The overall objectives of the Project for the Preparation of the Scaling up of the National Cadastre (PPMEC) are: 
Contribute to the security of land tenure for all segments of the Beninese population and to the promotion of private investments; 
Prepare the putting in place of the mechanism and the actors (national, PTFs and other actors in the chain) for the scaling up of the national cadastre. 
The expected outcomes are: 
-	The ANDF is able to manage, maintain and develop e-FB, adapted to the needs of Benin, in a sustainable way; 
-	The municipalities, notaries and surveyors play their role effectively in updating the cadastral data in the 12 municipalities; 
-	The competent national authorities take decisions on the legal and institutional arrangements required for the scaling up of the national cadastre; 
-	Civil society actors get better consideration of the interests of vulnerable groups when updating cadastral data.
